{"user": "In Othello endgames, if White secures 3 corners like that, is the game basically over, or can Black still fight back?", "user_ts": "2026-08-10T22:14:53.066355+00:00", "assistant": "Not automatically over \u2014 **3 corners doesn\u2019t mathematically guarantee a win** \u2014 but in most endgames it\u2019s a huge advantage because corners make adjacent edge discs stable.\n\nIn *this* final board, it was basically over once White got 3 corners **and** converted the edges:\n\n- White has **a1, h1, a8**\n- Black only has **h8**\n- Final count looks like **White 44, Black 20**\n\nBlack can still fight after losing 3 corners if there are enough empties left by:\n- forcing White to make bad moves,\n- winning mobility / passes,\n- taking the last corner,\n- maximizing final flips with parity.\n\nBut if the 3 corners also become stable full edges, like here, Black usually can\u2019t catch up.", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-10T22:14:53.066355+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-10T22:14:58.066355+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "consensus": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "votes": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 3, "Common Ground Question": 1}, "confidence": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 1.0, "Common Ground Question": 0.3333333333333333}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Knowledge Deficit Question", "Common Ground Question"], "llama": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "sonnet": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "General Principle"], "consensus": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "General Principle"], "votes": {"Board Report": 3, "General Principle": 3, "Local Justification": 2}, "confidence": {"Board Report": 1.0, "General Principle": 1.0, "Local Justification": 0.6666666666666666}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Board Report", "General Principle"], "llama": ["Board Re